The layer is binary (forest or non forest) and the something is wrong in the Summary of covariates (Min: 0, Max: 8911), likely an error on my part.  I got another suggestion from David Borchers which worked well for extracting values directly from the raster without using SpatialGridDataFrames.

xy = data.frame(x=maskWR10$x,y=maskWR10$y) # data frame of coordinates for which want to extract values
# (Here “mask” is a previously-created mask with the same coordinate system as ras.)
covariates(maskWR10)$spcov <- extract(rusty2, xy, spatial=TRUE) # extract at these coordinates and put them in the mask covariate named "spcov"

